<div style=3D"margin:0px">The draft has a number of nits and errors. Among =
others:<span>&nbsp;</span><br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px"><br>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin:0px">The related work section mentions KEYLESS and sub=
cert being complementary that is KEYLESS can perform the operations associa=
ted to the DC and/or those associated to the cert key. I do not think that =
is correct. KEYLESS does not support
 TLS 1.3 while DC only works with TLS 1.3. The LURK extension for TLS 1.3 [=
draft-mglt-lurk-tls13] should be mentioned instead. As LURK was mentioned d=
uring the adoption period and until version 05 that should not cause any is=
sues.&nbsp;<br>
</div>
